  "title": "tech_venture_and_ma_report.txt",
  "text": "Microsoft invested in OpenAI to expand enterprise artificial intelligence infrastructure. Satya Nadella serves as CEO of Microsoft in Redmond, Washington. Sam Altman co-founded OpenAI with Greg Brockman in San Francisco, California. OpenAI established a partnership with Apple to integrate conversational intelligence into consumer devices. Tim Cook leads Apple in Cupertino, California. Thrive Capital invested in OpenAI during its latest valuation round.\n\nPatrick Collison co-founded Stripe in San Francisco. Sequoia Capital backed Stripe across multiple venture capital rounds. Roelof Botha leads Sequoia Capital in Menlo Park, California. Stripe acquired Bridge to accelerate global payment settlements. Peter Thiel invested in Stripe during early financing rounds. Peter Thiel co-founded Founders Fund in San Francisco.\n\nMicrosoft acquired GitHub for $7.5 billion in an all-stock transaction. Databricks acquired MosaicML to strengthen generative model pre-training. Andreessen Horowitz invested in Databricks alongside Tiger Global. Marc Andreessen co-founded Andreessen Horowitz in Silicon Valley. Benchmark backed Uber in its initial funding stages. Dara Khosrowshahi serves as CEO of Uber in San Francisco.",
